<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Altai Mountains</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Altai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Altai Mountains are a mountain range in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> and Kazakhstan meet. The region was an important <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> and pastureland for nomadic peoples of the steppe. It is mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>'s profile in connection with the eastern lands contested during its decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/altai-mountains.jpg" alt="Altai Mountains" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rudyologist · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Altai_Mountains.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
